<h1 class="h4">How participation points work</h1><p>One award per activity. Edits and repeat clicks earn no extra points. Daily limits use South African calendar days. Unreliable historical dates or ownership are flagged rather than guessed.</p><div class="table-responsive"><table class="table"><thead><tr><th>Activity</th><th>Points</th><th>Awards per day</th><th>Minimum text length</th></tr></thead><tbody><?php foreach($pointPolicy['rules'] as $rule): ?><tr><td><?= \Portal\Html::escape($rule['label']) ?></td><td><?= $rule['points'] ?></td><td><?= $rule['limit'] ?></td><td><?= $rule['min']?:'—' ?></td></tr><?php endforeach; ?></tbody></table></div><p>Text length is a basic minimum, not an assessment of quality. Self-reactions do not score. Received assignments and leave requests are tracked at zero points. Page refreshes, password changes, notifications received, draft autosaves and destructive/moderation actions do not earn participation points.</p><p>Removing scored discussion content or undoing a completed checklist item reverses its original award. Restoring the same item restores only that award; it cannot earn again. Revoked awards still consume their original daily allocation, preventing delete-and-repost farming. Original report/submission awards are retained when records are archived.</p><p>Policy version <?= (int)$pointPolicy['version'] ?> applies to newly discovered events. Existing awards retain their original value. Corrections apply to the original activity date.</p>
